    "classification": "PROVED_LOWEST_INTERFACE_AND_SHARED_HIGHER_ROW_NECESSARY_CONDITIONS; NO_CANDIDATE; NOT_CLAY",
    "not_claimed": [
      "No realization of an integer geometry and shared data satisfying all conditions; no accepted finite two-step candidate.",
      "The two remaining independent higher complex components, other C directions and common template amplitude are not paid; next full-high-row-reduction work is excluded from this freeze.",
      "No new NS time window, local or uniform cross-generation infinite-dimensional error bound, uniform iteration, one fixed datum at infinitely many scales, finite total time, singularity or global regularity.",
      "Real-frequency finite algebra extensions are not arbitrary real-frequency Fourier data on the fixed torus; no exchange of forall N exists u0_N with exists u0 forall N.",
      "No repair of older failed computations, external novelty claim, human peer review or proof-assistant certification."
    ],
    "proved": [
      "For the original only-shortest-linear type, the complete lowest Z zero row uniquely fixes two sender real parts; complete lowest C is nonzero and has the original direction exactly under a real cubic and signed area relation.",
      "For every assumed admissible fixed geometry and given nonzero sender projections, the lowest conditions have a conditional solution with opposite nonzero sender areas. No admissible integer geometry is exhibited or asserted nonempty.",
      "Each higher zero row must pass a real quadratic projection condition with nonreal actual receiver ratio; its coefficients and both shared weights come from the same three seeds.",
      "The complete longest zero row forces the two higher seed areas to have the same sign. Together with the lowest complete C direction this requires c01*c02*C0<0, excluding the opposite-area branch and C0=0 but not all lowest roots.",
      "Given fixed geometry, a fixed lowest real representative and fixed higher projections satisfying the lowest real conditions, explicit positive area-square, signed-ratio-square and common positive lowest-amplitude equalities are equivalent to lowest complete conditions plus the two specified higher projections."
    ]
  },
